From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Fri, 12 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wayland-egl: install the client EGL integration private
 headers

Qt 6.10 moved the QtWayland client into qtbase and, in doing so, stopped
publishing the client-side EGL hardware integration as the private module
QtWaylandEglClientHwIntegration. The sources are now built as
QWaylandEglClientBufferPlugin only, which installs no headers.

The plugin does still export the types - QWaylandEglWindow and
QWaylandEglClientBufferIntegration carry Q_WAYLANDCLIENT_EXPORT, so the
plugin's .so exports their constructors, virtuals, vtables and typeinfo -
so an out-of-tree platform plugin can link against it. What it cannot do
is declare the types, because the headers are not installed.

webos-wayland-egl (qtwayland-webos) subclasses both of these to implement
the webOS platform integration. Install the four private headers so it can
see the declarations and link the implementation from the plugin, instead
of vendoring a copy of the sources that silently goes stale whenever the
qtbase SRCREV moves.

They install flat into QtWaylandClient/<version>/QtWaylandClient/private/,
next to the QtWaylandClient private headers they already include with
angle brackets; the quoted sibling includes between these four resolve in
that same directory.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS needs these to subclass out-of-tree]

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
---
 .../hardwareintegration/wayland-egl/CMakeLists.txt   | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/plugins/hardwareintegration/wayland-egl/CMakeLists.txt b/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/plugins/hardwareintegration/wayland-egl/CMakeLists.txt
index ff93adf..59aa2c6 100644
--- a/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/plugins/hardwareintegration/wayland-egl/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/plugins/platforms/wayland/plugins/hardwareintegration/wayland-egl/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -34,6 +34,20 @@ qt_internal_extend_target(QWaylandEglClientBufferPlugin CONDITION QT_FEATURE_egl
         QT_EGL_NO_X11
 )
 
+# webOS: publish the declarations for the types this plugin exports, so an
+# out-of-tree platform plugin can subclass QWaylandEglWindow and
+# QWaylandEglClientBufferIntegration and link the implementation from here.
+# Installed flat alongside the QtWaylandClient private headers, which is
+# where the angle-bracket includes in these files already point.
+install(FILES
+    qwaylandeglclientbufferintegration_p.h
+    qwaylandeglinclude_p.h
+    qwaylandeglwindow_p.h
+    qwaylandglcontext_p.h
+    DESTINATION
+        "${INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR}/QtWaylandClient/${PROJECT_VERSION}/QtWaylandClient/private"
+)
+
 
 #### Keys ignored in scope 1:.:.:wayland-egl.pro:<TRUE>:
 # OTHER_FILES = "wayland-egl.json"
